==English==

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{der|en|la|Carantania}}. Possibly of Celtic origin, compare {{cog|cel-pro|*karants||friend}}. The Latin toponym was also borrowed into Slavic as {{cog|sla-pro|*korǫtanъ}} (with an adjective {{cog|sla-pro|*korǫtьskъ}}), compare {{cog|cs|Korutany}} and {{cog|sl|Koroška||Carinthia}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kəˈrɪnθiə/}}<ref name="AHD">{{R:AHD}}</ref>
* {{hyphenation|en|Ca|rin|thia}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪnθiə|s=4}}

